# Mutation cases for W3C SCXML 3.10 + 3.11 — a `<history>` restores the cycle
# to where it was, on the Rust AOT path.
#
# Run with `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/ai_loop_history_rust.cases`.
#
# Sibling of `ai_loop_history_cpp.cases`, and since the Rust backend moved onto
# Appendix D (2026-09-24) the two are built the same way: C++ calls
# `SCE::Core::HistoryHelper::recordHistory` at run time, and the generated Rust
# policy's exit hook calls the runtime's `recorded_history`
# (`backends/rust/runtime/src/helpers/microstep.rs`) with the history's parent
# and its type. The filter that decides what a history records is the
# runtime's now, so that is what the cases below break.
#
# Until then the Rust emitter inlined the filter into the generated policy, and
# these cases mutated the committed `ai_loop_sm.rs`, whose anchor went with the
# inlined filter. The runtime is compiled into the `ai_loop` test binary, so a
# mutation of it changes the artifact the test runs — check 1 of the harness
# stays answerable — and the question is the one it always was: if the filter
# stopped recording a shallow history's children, would anything notice?

mutation_tests -p sce-rust-tests --test ai_loop
mutation_targets backends/rust/runtime/src/helpers/microstep.rs

# ── Shallow history records nothing ────────────────────────────────
#
# §scxml-3.10 has a shallow `<history>` record the active CHILDREN of its
# parent. A filter that matches nothing records an empty set, so re-entry falls
# back to the history's default and `resume` lands at the top of the cycle
# rather than where the person paused it.

mutation_case "shallow history records no state at all" <<'PY'
edit("backends/rust/runtime/src/helpers/microstep.rs",
     "doc.parent_of(state) == Some(parent)",
     "false && doc.parent_of(state) == Some(parent)")
PY

# ── Shallow history records the wrong states ───────────────────────
#
# The inverted comparison: keep everything except the parent's direct children.
# In a three-region `<parallel>` that is most of the rest of the configuration,
# so restoration re-enters states in regions the history state does not name.

mutation_case "shallow history records everything but the direct children" <<'PY'
edit("backends/rust/runtime/src/helpers/microstep.rs",
     "doc.parent_of(state) == Some(parent)",
     "doc.parent_of(state) != Some(parent)")
PY
